      "writtenOn": "2025-06-05T20:50:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Separating out comment about the constant 5...\n\nI really feel like this constant 5 may need to be configurable.\n\nIf so, will it work to configure it to 0? Meaning we immediately disable the connection from epoll rather than suspend any requests.\n\nI\u0027m concerned about the memory consumption from suspended requests.",
      "revId": "074cbff3115427b0e43d18c41f23acbf93b98fda",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "796f3b9f_e822d1ea",
        "filename": "src/MainNFSD/nfs_qos.c",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 1665,
      "author": {
        "id": 1038286
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-12T13:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes Frank, you are right, this value needs to be configurable.\nCurrently I have changes it to a MACRO, but in future will change it to configurable value from configuration file.\n\nMinimum configurable value should be 1 as per current implemnatation. Otherwise we have to keep the track if time when the recv is disable and enable it after 15 second. 1 entry in the queue avoids this timing calculation.",
      "parentUuid": "437f0645_0ab5353b",
      "revId": "074cbff3115427b0e43d18c41f23acbf93b98fda",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43dd9900_f736b9bc",
        "filename": "src/MainNFSD/nfs_qos.c",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 1665,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-13T23:56:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would like to at least see this configurable, ideally I\u0027d like to see the code handle the situation of setting it to 0 so we can experiment with different values. I\u0027m concerned that any suspending tasks will lead to excess memory usage.\n\nWe also need to explore whether this is sufficient, or if we really should do pre-decode and make QoS decisions before reading a complete request from the socket which could engage TCP back-pressure earloer.",
      "parentUuid": "796f3b9f_e822d1ea",
      "revId": "074cbff3115427b0e43d18c41f23acbf93b98fda",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
