        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-05T20:50:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we need this? The gsh_client isn\u0027t going away, client may start a new session, we shouldn\u0027t flush the QoS data.\n\nAlso, client can have multiple sessions per clientid",
      "revId": "074cbff3115427b0e43d18c41f23acbf93b98fda",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad9dd8bb_dea008d0",
        "filename": "src/Protocols/NFS/nfs4_op_destroy_session.c",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 109,
      "author": {
        "id": 1038286
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-12T13:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What i have seen in the testing is, this path gets called only if last session of client needs to be deleted.\nIn testing : I had 2 mount points mounted on same client (export1, export2). this path gets triggred only on 2nd umount and not 1st umount.\n\nI will recheck on this again. -Noted",
      "parentUuid": "2aa5b1e0_0ae95057",
      "revId": "074cbff3115427b0e43d18c41f23acbf93b98fda",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fbc00c45_54415b19",
        "filename": "src/Protocols/NFS/nfs4_op_destroy_session.c",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 109,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-13T23:56:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Clients may CREATE and DESTROY sessions for a number of reasons while still having connections. Per the RFC, it is not only used when the client is done with the server. So we definitely should not release QoS resources at this time.\n\nI\u0027m not sure if we have anything to release gsh_client structures for clients that have no activity, but that may be something to look into.",
      "parentUuid": "ad9dd8bb_dea008d0",
      "revId": "074cbff3115427b0e43d18c41f23acbf93b98fda",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c2feb43a_5fc85382",
        "filename": "src/Protocols/NFS/nfs4_op_destroy_session.c",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 109,
      "author": {
        "id": 1038286
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T16:19:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since after initation of destroy_session by client, socket also gets cloesed, in this qos_class_t should be freed. If required we create this structure at runtime fi new gsh_client get allocated.\n\ncheck_session_conn :SESSIONS :F_DBG :Comparing addr ::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830 for OP_SEQUENCE to Session bound addr ::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830\nfree_nfs_request :DISP :DEBUG :SVC_DECODE on 0x7fffcc001b90 fd 19 (::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830) xid\u003d3413674764 returned XPRT_IDLE\ncheck_session_conn :SESSIONS :F_DBG :Comparing addr ::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830 for OP_DESTROY_SESSION to Session bound addr ::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830\nqos_free_mem :QOS :DEBUG :trying to free from all exports CI: ::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830\nqos_drain_ios :QOS :DEBUG :qos_drain_ios CI: ::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830\nfree_nfs_request :DISP :DEBUG :SVC_DECODE on 0x7fffcc001b90 fd 19 (::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830) xid\u003d3430451980 returned XPRT_IDLE\nfree_nfs_request :DISP :DEBUG :SVC_DECODE on 0x7fffcc001b90 fd 19 (::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830) xid\u003d3447229196 returned XPRT_IDLE\ndissociate_custom_data_from_xprt :XPRT :DEBUG :About to un-reference custom-data from xprt with FD: 19, socket-addr: ::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830\ndissociate_custom_data_from_xprt :XPRT :DEBUG :Done dissociating custom-data for xprt with FD: 19, socket-addr: ::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830\ndestroy_custom_data_for_destroyed_xprt :XPRT :DEBUG :Processing custom data for destroyed xprt: 0x7fffcc001b90 with FD: 19, socket-addr: ::ffff:XX.X.XXX.XX:830",
      "parentUuid": "fbc00c45_54415b19",
      "revId": "074cbff3115427b0e43d18c41f23acbf93b98fda",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "44bdb39a_93e11b68",
        "filename": "src/Protocols/NFS/nfs4_op_destroy_session.c",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 109,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T21:20:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no protocol requirement that the client close the socket after DESTROY_SESSION. It may be true that the Linux client always does, or at least you have observed that behavior, but clients may not behave that way and that should not be a reason to free the QoS resources.\n\nA client can call CREATE_SESSION multiple times to create multiple sessions, and may call DESTROY_SESSION to reduce the number of sessions while still being active.",
      "parentUuid": "c2feb43a_5fc85382",
      "revId": "074cbff3115427b0e43d18c41f23acbf93b98fda",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
